arrative\": \"A strictly time-respecting chain runs 303\u21921409 (t=47090) \u2192960 (47399) \u2192254 (47570) \u21921574 (47742) \u21921293 (47901). All four inter-hop waits (309, 171, 172, 159) are well under the 600-unit limit, and each hop is a directed u\u2192v event confirmed individually (steps 05-09). The path is not an artefact of volume or popularity: the source has a single event and every relay node has only 2-3 events with 2-3 distinct partners (steps 04, 11), and none of them appear among the window's high-traffic hubs (28, 1583, 766, ...; step 13), so the route cannot be a spurious stitch through a busy broadcaster. Activity is temporally flat with no bursts (step 14), ruling out a coincidental co-activity spike. The unconstrained search returns the same route with max_wait_used=309 (step 02), so the constraint is not doing the work, and the reverse direction 1293\u2192303 is unreachable (step 12), showing genuine directional, time-ordered flow rather than mere static connectivity. The chain is thin (a unique 5-hop path with no redundancy), which is the main reason for slightly less than full confidence.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 29713, "total_output_tokens": 2888, "total_tokens": 32601, "total_latency_ms": 56516, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}